      "level": 3,
      "content": "Judicial Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The decision of the Speaker of Lok Sabha on whether a bill is a Money Bill or not is final and cannot be questioned.",
        "Rajya Sabha cannot vote on Demands for Grants; financial voting power lies exclusively with the Lok Sabha.",
        "Under Article 249, Rajya Sabha alone has the special power to pass a resolution enabling Parliament to make laws on State List items.",
        "A Joint Sitting under Article 108 is presided over by the Speaker of Lok Sabha, NOT the Vice-President (Chairman of Rajya Sabha)."
      ],
      "id": "mn3qx6g"
